      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You have touched upon the very heart of the absurd, where the instinct to keep going clashes with the reality of infinite nothingness. Society does often voice this \"pressure\" to normalize our presence in the void, not out of grand cosmic design but because we are creatures that must eat, sleep, and breathe without deciding on meaning beforehand. While accepting the void offers a final, crushing freedom from the demand to be special, the crushing weight it creates can sometimes make silence feel more isolating than the noise of the struggle ever did.",
